Alternative device trees
========================

Place compiled .dtb files directly in this directory for carrier boards that
use the same core module and base image. The interactive generator adds a
Device tree menu when at least one .dtb is present. The default entry uses
the base board name, such as mixtile-core3588e-v2, and keeps the device tree
supplied with the image.
Menu choices show the board names without the .dtb suffix.

The selected filename determines the output board name. For example,
vision1.dtb produces vision1.img and update bundles containing vision1 in
their filenames. The original base machine and RAUC compatibility identity
are retained.

Both the FIT device tree and the device tree embedded in resource.img are
replaced. Their original internal filenames are preserved for U-Boot.
Other resource entries, such as logos, are preserved. Input files are not
modified. Use --dtb PATH or the YAML dtb option for explicit commands.
